# Force LF on checkout on every OS. The golden snapshot
# (tests/golden/generated-manifest.sha256) is a BYTE hash of the generated tree;
# a checkout that converted source files to CRLF would change those bytes and
# break the byte-identical golden test. This is exercised on both CI legs of
# .github/workflows/generate-check.yml's `generate-check` matrix (ubuntu-latest
# and macos-latest) today; a hypothetical windows-latest leg would need it too,
# but no such leg exists yet. eol=lf keeps the working tree identical across
# platforms regardless of which of those actually run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The golden manifest itself and shipped content must never be CRLF-normalized.
tests/golden/generated-manifest.sha256 text eol=lf
